 that object. Ref history appeared rewound and omitted merged commit `2a93f180…`. `git fetch gerrit main` returned timeout/HTTP 504, and CI run `34235734839` failed checkout when Gerrit returned HTTP 502 fetching change 2834. The service later recovered: the parent became readable and ref advertisement worked again.\n\nA separate `/rebar-debug` session owns investigation. This ticket records the incident only; the comment-remediation epic must continue without debugging Gerrit here.\n\n## Plan\n- Reconstruct the Gerrit ref and object-availability timeline from durable server and CI evidence.\n- Determine why an advertised parent was temporarily unreadable and why checkout/fetch returned 502/504.\n- Prove the root cause before proposing a fix, following `/rebar-debug`.\n- Add regression or operational safeguards appropriate to the confirmed failure class.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The incident timeline is supported by exact Gerrit and CI evidence.\n- [ ] A reproducible or otherwise proven root cause explains the ref/object inconsistency and 502/504 responses.\n- [ ] The failure-class remediation is implemented or a concrete operator runbook is documented.\n- [ ] Verification evidence demonstrates the remediation.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["gerrit","infra","debug"],"ticket_id":"93e5-b934-b2ec-43d2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Investigate transient Gerrit ref inconsistency and checkout 502","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4d251eae-c060-492d-aa52-0b59e4ed9802","f7942ba2-4b88-4f69-83d8-f2571d3f5943"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788900186481698001,"uuid":"b8fb1655-c62a-47d9-af93-cf08c0f